# 🛡️ Operating System Security

## 📌 Overview

This module focuses on understanding operating system security, common vulnerabilities, and techniques used to protect systems from unauthorized access and malicious activities.

As part of my cybersecurity learning journey on TryHackMe, I explored the fundamentals of securing operating systems and understanding how attackers exploit weaknesses in system configurations.

## 🎯 Topics Covered

* Operating System Security Fundamentals
* User Accounts and Authentication
* File Permissions and Access Control
* System Hardening
* Common Operating System Vulnerabilities
* Security Updates and Patch Management
* Privilege Escalation Concepts
* Defensive Security Practices

## 🔍 Key Learning Outcomes

* Understood the importance of operating system security in cybersecurity.
* Learned how access permissions help protect sensitive files and resources.
* Gained awareness of common operating system security weaknesses.
* Understood the role of system hardening in reducing attack surfaces.
* Explored the importance of secure configurations and regular patching.
* Developed foundational knowledge useful for penetration testing and defensive security.

