| Skill                   | Description                                           |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| OS Security             | Understanding operating system protection mechanisms  |
| Access Control          | Managing permissions and user privileges              |
| System Hardening        | Reducing security risks through secure configurations |
| Vulnerability Awareness | Identifying common OS security weaknesses             |
| Defensive Security      | Understanding methods to protect systems              |

## 💡 Key Takeaways

Operating system security is a fundamental component of cybersecurity. Proper access control, system hardening, regular updates, and secure configurations play an important role in protecting systems against potential threats.

This module strengthened my understanding of how operating systems can be secured and assessed from both offensive and defensive security perspectives.

